body:
Given the following code (link https://getpsalm.org/r/0501a76a56):

```php
<?php

class B {}

class A {
    public function someThing(): B {
        try {
            /** @var object|object[] **/
            $jsonTimeslotsAndTypes = array();

            if (is_array($jsonTimeslotsAndTypes) === true) {
                throw new Exception();
            }

            return new B();
        } catch (Exception $exception) {
            $previous = $exception->getPrevious();

            $failureReason = $previous ?
                get_class($previous) :
                get_class($exception);

            throw $exception;
        } finally {
            $tags = [
                'success' => isset($exception) ? 'false' : 'true'
            ];

            var_dump(isset($failureReason));
            var_dump(isset($exception));
        }
    }
}
```

Psalm (up to dev-master) reports the following issues (and a valid `ForbiddenCode` for the `var_dump`):

```
ERROR: UndefinedVariable - 26:36 - Cannot find referenced variable $exception
ERROR: UndefinedVariable - 29:22 - Cannot find referenced variable $failureReason
INFO: UnusedVariable - 19:13 - Variable $failureReason is never referenced
INFO: UnusedVariable - 25:13 - Variable $tags is never referenced
```

All of these appear to be false positives though. `$exception` and `$failureReason` may or may not be available and they are reference after creation.
